# PlasticOS Zero-Stub Law

Do not ship placeholder behavior as delivered work.

A delivered method must not use `pass`, an empty success return (`[]`, `{}`, `0.0`, or `True`) in place of the real result, `NotImplementedError`, or a log line that says `NOT IMPLEMENTED`.

A change that alters behavior needs a regression check for the behavior that actually changed.
